mat (e.g., ASCII grid with `|` and `-`) and exact error-message wording are left to the implementation, as they do not affect correctness.\n\n## Risk-relevant context\n\n- Touches: A new, standalone Go terminal application with no network access, no file I/O beyond terminal stdin/stdout, and no external dependencies.\n- Does not touch: Any existing production code, credentials, entitlements, identity, network services, persistent storage, or configuration infrastructure.\n\n## Risk tier\n0\n\n## Review\n\nAn agent drafts this document. The human approves or rejects it at the spec-review workflow gate with `wctl task decide <task> spec-review`, optionally using `--reject --feedback 'changes needed'`."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791815475755}}
